        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "8c776a68-153e-5a8d-92fa-4e6349846ffa",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Rhinelander Waldo, William Jay Gaynor, Providenza Panno, Kate Leone, Rosaria Maltese\n- Roles: New York City Fire Commissioner, New York City Police Commissioner\n- Events: Triangle Shirtwaist Factory fire\n- Places: New York City\n\nFacts:\n- Rhinelander Waldo was born on May 24, 1877, and died on August 13, 1927.\n- Mayor William Jay Gaynor appointed Rhinelander Waldo the seventh New York City Fire Commissioner on January 13, 1910.\n- Rhinelander Waldo resigned as New York City Fire Commissioner on May 23, 1911, less than two months after the Triangle Shirtwaist Factory fire, to accept appointment as the eighth New York City Police Commissioner.\n- Most victims of the Triangle Shirtwaist Factory fire were recent Italian and Jewish immigrant women aged 16 to 23.\n- Among Triangle Shirtwaist Factory fire victims with known ages, Providenza Panno was the oldest at 43, and Kate Leone and \"Sara\" Rosaria Maltese were the youngest at 14.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "0f352dbc-b285-512b-a192-9ab0d96676fc",
        "text": "Page: Rhinelander Waldo. Sentence: Rhinelander Waldo (May 24, 1877 – August 13, 1927) was appointed the seventh New York City Fire Commissioner by Mayor William Jay Gaynor on January 13, 1910.\nPage: Rhinelander Waldo. Sentence: He resigned on May 23, 1911, less than two months after the deadly Triangle Shirtwaist Factory fire to accept an appointment as the eighth New York City Police Commissioner.\nPage: Triangle Shirtwaist Factory fire. Sentence: Most of the victims were recent Italian and Jewish immigrant women aged 16 to 23; of the victims whose ages are known, the oldest victim was Providenza Panno at 43, and the youngest were 14-year-olds Kate Leone and \"Sara\" Rosaria Maltese.",
